.TH EPUB-SHRINK 1 "October 2026" "epub-shrink 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
epub-shrink \- shrink EPUB images for 1-bit e-ink readers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B epub-shrink
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIINPUT\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B epub-shrink
rewrites every raster image inside an EPUB as an 8-bit grayscale baseline
JPEG, downscaled so its longest side fits the panel of XTEInk devices
running CrossInk firmware (800x480 at 1 bit with dithering), then repacks
the archive with the
.I mimetype
entry first and uncompressed, as the EPUB specification requires.
When an image changes extension (PNG/GIF to JPEG), the OPF manifest entry
and every src/href/url() reference in the content documents are rewritten
to match.
.PP
Each
.I INPUT
may be an EPUB file or a directory, which is searched recursively for
.B *.epub
files.
By default each input file is
.B overwritten in place
(atomically, via a temporary file in the same directory).
Use
.B \-\-suffix
or
.B \-\-output\-dir
to keep the originals.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-suffix " \fISUFFIX\fR"
Write each result as \fINAME\fR\fISUFFIX\fR.epub next to the original
instead of overwriting it. A leading dot is added if missing, so
.B \-\-suffix .shrunk
and
.B \-\-suffix shrunk
both turn Book.epub into Book.shrunk.epub. When a directory is scanned,
files already carrying the suffix are skipped.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output\-dir " \fIDIR\fR"
Write optimized books into \fIDIR\fR (created if needed) instead of
overwriting the originals.
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-dim " \fIPIXELS\fR"
Longest image side in pixels. The default of 800 fits the XTEInk 800x480
panel in either orientation.
.TP
.BR \-\-quality " \fIN\fR"
JPEG quality, 1-95 (default: 60, visually transparent after 1-bit
dithering).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Report the outcome for every image in each book.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 if no EPUB files were found or any book failed to process.
.SH EXAMPLES
Shrink one book in place:
.PP
.nf
.RS
epub-shrink Book.epub
.RE
.fi
.PP
Keep the originals, writing Book.shrunk.epub alongside:
.PP
.nf
.RS
epub-shrink --suffix .shrunk Book.epub
.RE
.fi
.PP
Optimize a whole library onto a device:
.PP
.nf
.RS
epub-shrink -o /media/you/XTEINK/books/ ~/calibre-library/
.RE
.fi
